                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I've played this game (the first episode only) in 2017, when this silly little hobby of mine became my passion. I played o so many great, life changing games that year and, while I don't quite consider The Lion's Song among these, it certainly helped me to see games as much more than what the triple A landscape had to offer.\n\nThe moments of finding inspiration to a work of art one's working towards is so beautifully captured here —and while I would like it to last a lot longer so we as players would have more time to connect with Wilma, and to live her artistic and personal struggles, and I find it a bit idealistic— although what it does make right blows its issues out of the water. I'm no musician, I'm barely a writer, but finding those moments when anything can make a connection in your mind to help you advance in something you're creating is so well captured that I cannot help but love this 30~ish minutes long point and click adventure.",
